#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adapt to changes in installing and depending on Qiskit v1.0"
msgstr ""
"Sesuaikan diri dengan perubahan dalam pemasangan dan kebergantungan pada "
"Qiskit v1.0"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install the new Qiskit v1.0 package"
msgstr "Pasang pakej Qiskit v1.0 yang baharu"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore jupyterlab, testenv */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore jupyterlab, testenv */}\n"

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Install the new Qiskit v1.0 package {#install-the-new-qiskit-v10-package}"
msgstr ""
"Pasang pakej Qiskit v1.0 yang baharu {#install-the-new-qiskit-v10-package}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Qiskit v1.0 uses a different packaging structure than previous Qiskit "
"versions and will likely cause problems in environments that use packages "
"that are not ready for Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Qiskit v1.0 menggunakan struktur pakej yang berbeza berbanding versi Qiskit "
"sebelumnya dan berkemungkinan besar akan menyebabkan masalah dalam "
"persekitaran yang menggunakan pakej yang belum bersedia untuk Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Do not try to upgrade an existing Python virtual environment to Qiskit v1.0 in-place.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Jangan cuba naik taraf persekitaran maya Python yang sedia ada ke Qiskit v1.0 secara langsung.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will not make similar breaking packaging changes in the future. This is a one-time event, at the release of Qiskit v1.0, specifically so that our packaging story will be as easy as possible in the future.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Kami tidak akan membuat perubahan pakej yang memecahkan keserasian seperti ini pada masa hadapan. Ini adalah peristiwa sekali sahaja, pada masa pelepasan Qiskit v1.0, khusus supaya cerita pakej kami akan semudah mungkin pada masa hadapan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This guide is divided into the following sections.  You only need to review "
"the sections that are relevant to you.\n"
msgstr ""
"Panduan ini dibahagikan kepada bahagian-bahagian berikut. Anda hanya perlu "
"menyemak bahagian yang berkaitan dengan anda.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Users should read the [For users](#for-users) section.\n"
msgstr "Pengguna perlu membaca bahagian [Untuk pengguna](#for-users).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you develop or maintain a package that depends on Qiskit, read the [For "
"developers](#for-developers) section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika anda membangun atau menyelenggara pakej yang bergantung pada Qiskit, "
"baca bahagian [Untuk pembangun](#for-developers).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you encounter problems installing or importing Qiskit v1.0, review the "
"[Troubleshooting](#troubleshooting) section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika anda menghadapi masalah memasang atau mengimport Qiskit v1.0, semak "
"bahagian [Penyelesaian masalah](#troubleshooting).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are interested in understanding the old package structure and why it "
"changed, review the [overview of the breaking package "
"changes](/guides/metapackage-migration).\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika anda berminat untuk memahami struktur pakej lama dan sebab ia berubah, "
"semak [gambaran keseluruhan perubahan pakej yang memecahkan "
"keserasian](/guides/metapackage-migration).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"for-users\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"for-users\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For users {#for-users}"
msgstr "Untuk pengguna {#for-users}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You must start a new virtual environment to install Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"It is very tricky and error-prone to upgrade an existing installation in-place to Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda mesti memulakan persekitaran maya baharu untuk memasang Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Sangat rumit dan mudah terdedah kepada ralat untuk menaik taraf pemasangan sedia ada secara langsung ke Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The examples in this section use the `venv` module that is part of the Python standard library.\n"
"If you use a different tool, such as `virtualenv` or `conda`, consult its documentation for help.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Contoh dalam bahagian ini menggunakan modul `venv` yang merupakan sebahagian daripada pustaka standard Python.\n"
"Jika anda menggunakan alat yang berbeza, seperti `virtualenv` atau `conda`, rujuk dokumentasinya untuk mendapatkan bantuan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For Linux and macOS commands, a bash-like syntax is used.\n"
"PowerShell is used for Windows commands.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk arahan Linux dan macOS, sintaks seperti bash digunakan.\n"
"PowerShell digunakan untuk arahan Windows.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"creating-a-venv\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"creating-a-venv\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Create the new environment {#create-the-new-environment}"
msgstr "Cipta persekitaran baharu {#create-the-new-environment}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create a new virtual environment in each project directory you're working "
"in, using your preferred version of Python 3.8 or later.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cipta persekitaran maya baharu dalam setiap direktori projek yang anda "
"kerjakan, menggunakan versi Python 3.8 atau lebih baharu yang anda pilih.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"          <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"
msgstr ""
"        <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"          <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```bash\n"
"             python3 -m venv .venv\n"
"             ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```bash\n"
"             python3 -m venv .venv\n"
"             ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "          <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"
msgstr "          <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "          <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"
msgstr "          <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            ```powershell\n"
"            python -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"            ```powershell\n"
"            python -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<span id=\"activate\"></span>\n"
"2. Activate the environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"<span id=\"activate\"></span>\n"
"2. Aktifkan persekitaran tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```bash\n"
"             source .venv/bin/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```bash\n"
"             source .venv/bin/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            ```powershell\n"
"            .venv\\Scripts\\activate.ps1\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"            ```powershell\n"
"            .venv\\Scripts\\activate.ps1\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Install packages as desired.\n"
"You should do this by using only one `pip install` command with all the dependencies on it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pasang pakej mengikut keperluan.\n"
"Anda patut melakukan ini dengan menggunakan hanya satu arahan `pip install` dengan semua kebergantungan di dalamnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   You can optionally include additional packages by including them as "
"arguments.  For example:\n"
msgstr ""
"   Anda boleh memasukkan pakej tambahan secara pilihan dengan menyertakannya"
" sebagai argumen. Contohnya:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Qiskit v1.0 includes breaking changes, so several packages are marked as "
"not-yet-compatible with it.  Therefore, you might see errors from `pip` "
"until new versions of those packages are released. Old versions of packages "
"might also depend on the legacy `qiskit-terra` package.  Such packages might"
" not return errors when running this command, but might raise an error when "
"running `import qiskit`.  You should not install any packages that depend "
"directly on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Qiskit v1.0 merangkumi perubahan yang memecahkan keserasian, jadi "
"beberapa pakej ditanda sebagai belum serasi dengannya. Oleh itu, anda "
"mungkin akan melihat ralat daripada `pip` sehingga versi baharu pakej "
"tersebut dikeluarkan. Versi lama pakej mungkin juga bergantung pada pakej "
"legasi `qiskit-terra`. Pakej sedemikian mungkin tidak mengembalikan ralat "
"semasa menjalankan arahan ini, tetapi mungkin akan menimbulkan ralat semasa "
"menjalankan `import qiskit`. Anda tidak patut memasang sebarang pakej yang "
"bergantung secara langsung pada `qiskit-terra`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"   One way to require `pip` to forbid `qiskit-terra` from individual `install` commands is to use [a constraints file](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/user_guide/#constraints-files) that requires that `qiskit-terra` is set to an impossible version.\n"
"   For example, a constraints file that includes the line `qiskit-terra>=1.0` will mean that if a dependency attempts to install `qiskit-terra`, no published versions will match the requirements.\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"   Salah satu cara untuk meminta `pip` melarang `qiskit-terra` daripada arahan `install` individu adalah dengan menggunakan [fail kekangan](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/user_guide/#constraints-files) yang menetapkan `qiskit-terra` pada versi yang mustahil.\n"
"   Contohnya, fail kekangan yang mengandungi baris `qiskit-terra>=1.0` bermakna jika kebergantungan cuba memasang `qiskit-terra`, tiada versi yang diterbitkan akan memenuhi keperluan tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   We have provided such a file in a GitHub Gist at "
"[https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints](https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints), which "
"you can use like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kami telah menyediakan fail sedemikian dalam GitHub Gist di "
"[https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints](https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints), yang "
"boleh anda gunakan seperti berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   If a package requires `qiskit-terra`, you will see [a resolution failure](#pip-resolution-impossible).\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"   Jika sesebuah pakej memerlukan `qiskit-terra`, anda akan melihat [kegagalan resolusi](#pip-resolution-impossible).\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"   Do not install packages that are incompatible with Qiskit v1.0 on this virtual environment.  If you need to use such packages, install them in a separate virtual environment with Qiskit 0.45 or 0.46.\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"   Jangan pasang pakej yang tidak serasi dengan Qiskit v1.0 pada persekitaran maya ini. Jika anda perlu menggunakan pakej sedemikian, pasangnya dalam persekitaran maya berasingan dengan Qiskit 0.45 atau 0.46.\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   If you have an existing environment, you can use "
"[`pipdeptree`](https://github.com/tox-"
"dev/pipdeptree/blob/main/README.md#pipdeptree) to query the requirements of "
"your installed packages to see if they require `qiskit<1`.  For any that "
"require `qiskit<1`, check for updates that make it compatible with Qiskit "
"v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Jika anda mempunyai persekitaran sedia ada, anda boleh menggunakan "
"[`pipdeptree`](https://github.com/tox-"
"dev/pipdeptree/blob/main/README.md#pipdeptree) untuk membuat pertanyaan "
"keperluan pakej yang dipasang bagi melihat sama ada ia memerlukan "
"`qiskit<1`. Bagi mana-mana yang memerlukan `qiskit<1`, semak kemaskini yang "
"menjadikannya serasi dengan Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   If you encounter issues, consult the [troubleshooting](#troubleshooting) "
"section, or ask on [Qiskit Slack](https://qisk.it/join-slack). If you think "
"there is a bug, you can [create an issue against "
"Qiskit](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/issues/new/choose).\n"
msgstr ""
"   Jika anda menghadapi masalah, rujuk bahagian [penyelesaian "
"masalah](#troubleshooting), atau tanya di [Qiskit "
"Slack](https://qisk.it/join-slack). Jika anda rasa ada pepijat, anda boleh "
"[membuat isu terhadap "
"Qiskit](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/issues/new/choose).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are not planning to use the environment immediately, use the "
"`deactivate` command to leave it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika anda tidak merancang untuk menggunakan persekitaran itu segera, gunakan"
" arahan `deactivate` untuk keluar daripadanya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"activating-a-venv\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"activating-a-venv\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Use the new environment {#use-the-new-environment}"
msgstr "Gunakan persekitaran baharu {#use-the-new-environment}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each time you start a new command line session, you must navigate to your "
"project directory and \"activate\" the environment by running the `activate`"
" command:\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap kali anda memulakan sesi baris arahan baharu, anda mesti pergi ke "
"direktori projek anda dan \"aktifkan\" persekitaran dengan menjalankan "
"arahan `activate`:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"for-developers\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"for-developers\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For developers {#for-developers}"
msgstr "Untuk pembangun {#for-developers}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you maintain a package that depends on Qiskit, use this information to "
"learn how to correctly express your compatibility and test against Qiskit "
"v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika anda menyelenggara pakej yang bergantung pada Qiskit, gunakan maklumat "
"ini untuk mengetahui cara menyatakan keserasian anda dengan betul dan "
"menguji terhadap Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Recommendations for requirements {#recommendations-for-requirements}"
msgstr "Cadangan untuk keperluan {#recommendations-for-requirements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We recommend that your package requires `qiskit>=0.45,<1` (or other appropriate lower bound) if you are not certain whether the package is compatible with Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"This is [the same recommendation being made for NumPy 2.0 compatibility](https://github.com/numpy/numpy/issues/24300).\n"
msgstr ""
"Kami mengesyorkan agar pakej anda memerlukan `qiskit>=0.45,<1` (atau had bawah lain yang sesuai) jika anda tidak pasti sama ada pakej itu serasi dengan Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Ini adalah [cadangan yang sama yang dibuat untuk keserasian NumPy 2.0](https://github.com/numpy/numpy/issues/24300).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A Qiskit v1.0 release candidate, version 1.0.0rc1, will be released on 1 February 2024.\n"
"You should test your package against this, and as soon as possible, release a new (compatible) version of your package with its upper requirement unpinned.\n"
msgstr ""
"Calon pelepasan Qiskit v1.0, versi 1.0.0rc1, akan dikeluarkan pada 1 Februari 2024.\n"
"Anda patut menguji pakej anda terhadap ini, dan secepat mungkin, keluarkan versi baharu (yang serasi) pakej anda dengan keperluan atasan yang tidak ditetapkan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recommendations for testing against Qiskit v1.0 {#recommendations-for-"
"testing-against-qiskit-v10}"
msgstr ""
"Cadangan untuk pengujian terhadap Qiskit v1.0 {#recommendations-for-testing-"
"against-qiskit-v10}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These recommendations apply to testing proactively against the Qiskit `main`"
" branch, and to testing against the v1.0.0rc1 (and later, if applicable) "
"release candidate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cadangan ini digunakan untuk pengujian secara proaktif terhadap cawangan "
"`main` Qiskit, dan untuk pengujian terhadap calon pelepasan v1.0.0rc1 (dan "
"kemudian, jika berkenaan).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We do not recommend initially branch-protecting on CI success against the Qiskit `main` branch because Qiskit changes could prevent you from merging PRs.\n"
"After the release of Qiskit release candidates, and after all of your package's dependencies support Qiskit v1.0, we *do* recommend branch-protecting on success against the latest release candidate, to ensure that the package remains compatible with Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kami tidak mengesyorkan perlindungan cawangan pada kejayaan CI terhadap cawangan `main` Qiskit pada mulanya kerana perubahan Qiskit boleh menghalang anda daripada menggabungkan PR.\n"
"Selepas pelepasan calon pelepasan Qiskit, dan selepas semua kebergantungan pakej anda menyokong Qiskit v1.0, kami *mengesyorkan* perlindungan cawangan pada kejayaan terhadap calon pelepasan terkini, bagi memastikan pakej kekal serasi dengan Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If neither your package, nor any of its transitive dependencies, has a requirement pin on `qiskit<1`, you should create a testing virtual environment as you normally would, in a single `pip install` command, and directly specify `qiskit==1.0.0rc1` or `qiskit==git+https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit.git@main` as appropriate.\n"
"This is the most reliable way to ensure that you have a completely valid environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika bukan pakej anda, mahupun mana-mana kebergantungan transitif anda, mempunyai pin keperluan pada `qiskit<1`, anda patut mencipta persekitaran maya pengujian seperti biasa, dalam satu arahan `pip install`, dan secara langsung menyatakan `qiskit==1.0.0rc1` atau `qiskit==git+https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit.git@main` mengikut kesesuaian.\n"
"Ini adalah cara paling boleh dipercayai untuk memastikan anda mempunyai persekitaran yang sepenuhnya sah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the only component of your package's dependency graph that has a requirement pin on `qiskit<1` is your own package, you might want to have your CI suite first temporarily patch your requirements file to allow Qiskit v1.0, and then install the environment in a single step as before.\n"
"Alternatively, use the following rules for general-purpose environment upgrades, but switch to single-environment resolution as soon as feasible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika satu-satunya komponen graf kebergantungan pakej anda yang mempunyai pin keperluan pada `qiskit<1` adalah pakej anda sendiri, anda mungkin mahu suite CI anda terlebih dahulu menampal sementara fail keperluan anda untuk membenarkan Qiskit v1.0, kemudian pasang persekitaran dalam satu langkah seperti sebelumnya.\n"
"Sebagai alternatif, gunakan peraturan berikut untuk naik taraf persekitaran tujuan umum, tetapi beralih ke resolusi persekitaran tunggal secepat mungkin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If at least one of your transitive dependencies does not yet have a release version that allows Qiskit v1.0 support, you must make manual changes.\n"
"There are several strategies to try, in approximate order of preference (most preferable to least):\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika sekurang-kurangnya satu daripada kebergantungan transitif anda belum mempunyai versi pelepasan yang membenarkan sokongan Qiskit v1.0, anda mesti membuat perubahan manual.\n"
"Terdapat beberapa strategi untuk dicuba, dalam susunan keutamaan kira-kira (paling diutamakan ke paling kurang):\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Install the problematic dependency from its own `main` branch, if its "
"development version has relaxed the pin, so you can build the test "
"environment in a single step.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pasang kebergantungan yang bermasalah daripada cawangan `main` sendiri, jika"
" versi pembangunannya telah melonggarkan pin, supaya anda boleh membina "
"persekitaran ujian dalam satu langkah.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Exclude the use of that dependency from the test environment, if possible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kecualikan penggunaan kebergantungan itu daripada persekitaran ujian, jika "
"boleh.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create a test environment in the same way you would normally, and then "
"manually override it to use Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cipta persekitaran ujian dengan cara yang sama seperti biasanya, kemudian "
"gantikan secara manual untuk menggunakan Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Manually upgrade an existing environment {#manually-upgrade-an-existing-"
"environment}"
msgstr ""
"Naik taraf persekitaran sedia ada secara manual {#manually-upgrade-an-"
"existing-environment}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"This process deliberately creates an invalid environment.  Therefore, any test using it is less valid. Tests might appear to pass, but this does not guarantee that the package is compatible with Qiskit v1.0.  This could happen because the environment is not self-consistent and could contain files that do not exist in a valid environment, or the behavior of an overridden package might change with Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Proses ini dengan sengaja mencipta persekitaran yang tidak sah. Oleh itu, sebarang ujian yang menggunakannya adalah kurang sah. Ujian mungkin kelihatan lulus, tetapi ini tidak menjamin bahawa pakej itu serasi dengan Qiskit v1.0. Ini boleh berlaku kerana persekitaran tidak konsisten sendiri dan mungkin mengandungi fail yang tidak wujud dalam persekitaran yang sah, atau tingkah laku pakej yang digantikan mungkin berubah dengan Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"If one of your dependencies pins `qiskit<1` even on their development branch, it might not work in any way with Qiskit v1.0, and if your tests cannot run because of this, you might have to wait for them (or work with them) to become compatible.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Jika salah satu kebergantungan anda meletakkan pin `qiskit<1` walaupun pada cawangan pembangunan mereka, ia mungkin tidak berfungsi dalam apa jua cara dengan Qiskit v1.0, dan jika ujian anda tidak dapat dijalankan kerana ini, anda mungkin perlu menunggu mereka (atau bekerjasama dengan mereka) untuk menjadi serasi.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To upgrade an environment in situ, follow these steps:\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menaik taraf persekitaran secara langsung, ikuti langkah-langkah "
"ini:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create an environment as usual, ensuring that there are no packages that "
"extend the `qiskit` or `qiskit.providers` namespace installed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cipta persekitaran seperti biasa, pastikan tiada pakej yang meluaskan ruang "
"nama `qiskit` atau `qiskit.providers` yang dipasang.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Uninstall both `qiskit` and `qiskit-terra` to make sure that neither is "
"present:\n"
msgstr ""
"Nyahpasang kedua-dua `qiskit` dan `qiskit-terra` untuk memastikan tiada satu"
" pun yang wujud:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  At this point, the environment's `site-packages` should not contain a `qiskit` directory. You don't need to verify this on every CI run, but if you are debugging a script locally, follow these steps to verify:\n"
"  1. Run the following command from within the `python` of the virtual environment:\n"
msgstr ""
"  Pada ketika ini, `site-packages` persekitaran tidak patut mengandungi direktori `qiskit`. Anda tidak perlu mengesahkan ini pada setiap jalankan CI, tetapi jika anda menyahpepijat skrip secara tempatan, ikuti langkah-langkah ini untuk mengesahkan:\n"
"  1. Jalankan arahan berikut dari dalam `python` persekitaran maya:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    import site\n"
"    print(site.getsitepackages())\n"
"    ```\n"
"  2. Verify that those directories do not contain a `qiskit` directory. If they do, you likely have namespace-extending packages installed, and you should find these and remove the dependency.\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```python\n"
"    import site\n"
"    print(site.getsitepackages())\n"
"    ```\n"
"  2. Sahkan bahawa direktori-direktori tersebut tidak mengandungi direktori `qiskit`. Jika ya, anda mungkin mempunyai pakej yang meluaskan ruang nama yang dipasang, dan anda patut mencari serta membuang kebergantungan tersebut.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install the target version of Qiskit v1.0 with one of these commands:\n"
msgstr "Pasang versi sasaran Qiskit v1.0 dengan salah satu arahan berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "After the  desired release candidate has been published:\n"
msgstr "Selepas calon pelepasan yang dikehendaki diterbitkan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install 'qiskit==1.0.0rc1'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  * For a `main`-branch dependency (or substitute whatever `git` revision identifier you prefer after the `@`).\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install 'qiskit==1.0.0rc1'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  * Untuk kebergantungan cawangan `main` (atau gantikan pengecam semakan `git` yang anda sukai selepas `@`).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install 'git+https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit.git@main'\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install 'git+https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit.git@main'\n"
"    ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You now have an environment that Qiskit allows you to test in. If `import "
"qiskit` results in an `ImportError`, or if you are struggling to find your "
"dependencies, see the advice in the section about the  [invalid-environment "
"protections](#qiskit-1.0-import-error) in Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda kini mempunyai persekitaran yang Qiskit benarkan anda untuk menguji "
"dalamnya. Jika `import qiskit` menghasilkan `ImportError`, atau jika anda "
"bergelut untuk mencari kebergantungan anda, lihat nasihat dalam bahagian "
"tentang [perlindungan persekitaran tidak sah](#qiskit-1.0-import-error) "
"dalam Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sample manual GitHub Actions workflows {#sample-manual-github-actions-"
"workflows}"
msgstr ""
"Contoh aliran kerja GitHub Actions manual {#sample-manual-github-actions-"
"workflows}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following workflows set up a scheduled job to run overnight.  This job "
"sets up a testing environment for Qiskit v1.0 and runs `pytest` (or whatever"
" test steps you need).\n"
msgstr ""
"Aliran kerja berikut menyediakan tugas berjadual untuk dijalankan pada waktu"
" malam. Tugas ini menyediakan persekitaran pengujian untuk Qiskit v1.0 dan "
"menjalankan `pytest` (atau langkah ujian apa pun yang anda perlukan).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For a package that has no transitive dependencies `qiskit<1`:\n"
msgstr "Untuk pakej yang tidak mempunyai kebergantungan transitif `qiskit<1`:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a package that has unavoidable transitive dependencies that pin "
"`qiskit<1`, build an invalid environment:\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk pakej yang mempunyai kebergantungan transitif yang tidak dapat "
"dielakkan yang meletakkan pin `qiskit<1`, bina persekitaran yang tidak "
"sah:\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Sample `tox` configuration {#sample-tox-configuration}"
msgstr "Contoh konfigurasi `tox` {#sample-tox-configuration}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following are examples of `tox.ini` sections to build a testing "
"environment for Qiskit v1.0 and run `pytest` (or whatever test steps you "
"need).\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah contoh bahagian `tox.ini` untuk membina persekitaran "
"pengujian bagi Qiskit v1.0 dan menjalankan `pytest` (atau langkah ujian apa "
"pun yang anda perlukan).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If nothing prevents Qiskit v1.0 from being installed in a valid "
"environment:\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika tiada yang menghalang Qiskit v1.0 daripada dipasang dalam persekitaran "
"yang sah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If your package or a transitive dependency has an unavoidable pin on `qiskit<1`, we recommend doing this testing using the manual environment construction as in the above section, because `tox` introduces several complexities by being more strict about environment isolation and installation order.\n"
"This is correct behavior by `tox` (we shouldn't construct an invalid environment), but because we already know we're building an invalid environment, these checks get in the way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika pakej anda atau kebergantungan transitif mempunyai pin yang tidak dapat dielakkan pada `qiskit<1`, kami mengesyorkan melakukan pengujian ini menggunakan pembinaan persekitaran manual seperti dalam bahagian di atas, kerana `tox` memperkenalkan beberapa kerumitan dengan menjadi lebih ketat tentang pengasingan persekitaran dan susunan pemasangan.\n"
"Ini adalah tingkah laku yang betul oleh `tox` (kita tidak patut membina persekitaran yang tidak sah), tetapi kerana kita sudah tahu kita sedang membina persekitaran yang tidak sah, pemeriksaan ini menghalang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"troubleshooting\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"troubleshooting\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting {#troubleshooting}"
msgstr "Penyelesaian masalah {#troubleshooting}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The packaging changes around Qiskit v1.0 are tricky, and Python's standard tool `pip` is not rich enough in some ways for us to communicate the changes in the distribution structures to it, which unfortunately might cause issues for users.\n"
"We have tried to make Qiskit fail quickly and loudly if it detects an invalid environment, without false positives.\n"
"We understand that users might find it annoying to get the error message, but in our experience, it's much better to be aware of the problem right away than for things to appear to be working on the surface, only to fail in subtle ways in the future.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perubahan pakej seputar Qiskit v1.0 agak rumit, dan alat standard Python `pip` tidak cukup kaya dalam beberapa aspek untuk kami menyampaikan perubahan dalam struktur pengedaran kepadanya, yang malangnya mungkin menyebabkan masalah kepada pengguna.\n"
"Kami telah cuba menjadikan Qiskit gagal dengan cepat dan lantang jika ia mengesan persekitaran yang tidak sah, tanpa positif palsu.\n"
"Kami faham bahawa pengguna mungkin mendapati mesej ralat itu menjengkelkan, tetapi berdasarkan pengalaman kami, jauh lebih baik untuk mengetahui masalah itu dengan segera daripada sesuatu kelihatan berfungsi di permukaan, tetapi akhirnya gagal secara halus pada masa hadapan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section contains packaging errors that you might see, and describes how"
" to resolve them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bahagian ini mengandungi ralat pakej yang mungkin anda lihat, dan "
"menerangkan cara menyelesaikannya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Most of these problems are not unique to Qiskit, so the advice is likely "
"relevant, even if the problematic parts are not related to Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kebanyakan masalah ini bukan unik kepada Qiskit, jadi nasihat ini mungkin "
"relevan, walaupun bahagian yang bermasalah tidak berkaitan dengan Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`import qiskit` says \"ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'qiskit'\" "
"{#import-qiskit-says-modulenotfounderror-no-module-named-qiskit}"
msgstr ""
"`import qiskit` memaparkan \"ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'qiskit'\""
" {#import-qiskit-says-modulenotfounderror-no-module-named-qiskit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Python cannot find your Qiskit installation.\n"
msgstr "Python tidak dapat mencari pemasangan Qiskit anda.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you definitely installed Qiskit, then you probably do not have the correct virtual environment activated.\n"
"See the [section on activating a virtual environment](#activating-a-venv) for instructions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika anda pasti telah memasang Qiskit, anda mungkin tidak mempunyai persekitaran maya yang betul yang diaktifkan.\n"
"Lihat [bahagian tentang mengaktifkan persekitaran maya](#activating-a-venv) untuk arahan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are using Jupyter and see this, ensure that Jupyter is installed into the same virtual environment as Qiskit.\n"
"Exit Jupyter, activate the Qiskit virtual environment on the command line, run `pip install jupyterlab` (or whichever notebook interface you use), then reopen Jupyter.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika anda menggunakan Jupyter dan melihat ini, pastikan Jupyter dipasang ke dalam persekitaran maya yang sama dengan Qiskit.\n"
"Keluar dari Jupyter, aktifkan persekitaran maya Qiskit pada baris arahan, jalankan `pip install jupyterlab` (atau antara muka notebook yang anda gunakan), kemudian buka semula Jupyter.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`import qiskit` succeeds, but trying to do anything returns "
"\"AttributeError: module 'qiskit' has no attribute '...'\" {#import-qiskit-"
"succeeds-but-trying-to-do-anything-returns-attributeerror-module-qiskit-has-"
"no-attribute}"
msgstr ""
"`import qiskit` berjaya, tetapi cuba melakukan apa-apa mengembalikan "
"\"AttributeError: module 'qiskit' has no attribute '...'\" {#import-qiskit-"
"succeeds-but-trying-to-do-anything-returns-attributeerror-module-qiskit-has-"
"no-attribute}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This likely means that your environment had an old version of Qiskit in it alongside a package that extended its namespace (such as old versions of Qiskit Aer, or the long-obsolete Qiskit IBM Q&reg; Provider), and then Qiskit was uninstalled.\n"
"The easiest thing to do is to start a new virtual environment, and only install recent, non-obsolete packages into it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini berkemungkinan bermakna persekitaran anda mempunyai versi Qiskit lama di dalamnya bersama pakej yang meluaskan ruang namanya (seperti versi lama Qiskit Aer, atau Qiskit IBM Q&reg; Provider yang sudah lapuk), kemudian Qiskit dinyahpasang.\n"
"Perkara termudah yang perlu dilakukan adalah memulakan persekitaran maya baharu, dan hanya memasang pakej terkini yang tidak lapuk ke dalamnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you have just started a new virtual environment, or you're sure that legacy packages are not the problem, make sure that your current working directory (the directory your shell session was in when you launched Python / Jupyter) does not contain a folder called `qiskit`.\n"
"Python's default rules search the current working directory very early in the search path when trying to `import` a module, so a directory with a duplicate name can cause import problems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika anda baru sahaja memulakan persekitaran maya baharu, atau anda pasti pakej legasi bukan masalahnya, pastikan direktori kerja semasa anda (direktori sesi shell anda semasa anda melancarkan Python / Jupyter) tidak mengandungi folder bernama `qiskit`.\n"
"Peraturan lalai Python mencari direktori kerja semasa sangat awal dalam laluan carian semasa cuba `import` sesuatu modul, jadi direktori dengan nama pendua boleh menyebabkan masalah import.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"pip-resolution-impossible\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"pip-resolution-impossible\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`pip` refuses to install some packages together {#pip-refuses-to-install-"
"some-packages-together}"
msgstr ""
"`pip` enggan memasang beberapa pakej bersama-sama {#pip-refuses-to-install-"
"some-packages-together}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After running a `pip install` command with many items on it, you might see "
"an error such as:\n"
msgstr ""
"Selepas menjalankan arahan `pip install` dengan banyak item, anda mungkin "
"melihat ralat seperti:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This describes a true resolution conflict; there is no valid way to install "
"all of these distributions at the same time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini menggambarkan konflik resolusi yang sebenar; tiada cara yang sah untuk "
"memasang semua pengedaran ini pada masa yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the context of Qiskit v1.0, this is likely because one of the distributions you are trying to install contains a requirement like `qiskit<1.0`.\n"
"This means that the developers of that distribution have marked it as not (yet) compatible with Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam konteks Qiskit v1.0, ini berkemungkinan kerana salah satu pengedaran yang anda cuba pasang mengandungi keperluan seperti `qiskit<1.0`.\n"
"Ini bermakna pembangun pengedaran tersebut telah menandakannya sebagai tidak (lagi) serasi dengan Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can (politely) ask those developers when they will release a new version of their package that is compatible with Qiskit v1.0, but first check that they have no open issue or pull request already asking for this wherever they accept comments.\n"
"Be mindful that this takes time; please give the developers a month or so to prepare new versions of their distributions!\n"
"Until then, you cannot install that distribution alongside Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"To continue using that distribution, create a new virtual environment and use Qiskit 0.45 or 0.46 (or whichever version it supports) alongside that other package.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda boleh (dengan sopan) bertanya kepada pembangun tersebut bila mereka akan mengeluarkan versi baharu pakej mereka yang serasi dengan Qiskit v1.0, tetapi terlebih dahulu semak sama ada mereka tidak mempunyai isu atau permintaan tarik terbuka yang sudah meminta ini di mana pun mereka menerima komen.\n"
"Ingatlah bahawa ini mengambil masa; sila beri pembangun sebulan lebih kurang untuk menyediakan versi baharu pengedaran mereka!\n"
"Sehingga itu, anda tidak boleh memasang pengedaran tersebut bersama Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Untuk terus menggunakan pengedaran tersebut, cipta persekitaran maya baharu dan gunakan Qiskit 0.45 atau 0.46 (atau versi yang disokongnya) bersama pakej lain itu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"If you get this error, **do not** try to build the environment by calling `pip install` several times.\n"
"Those commands will probably not fail, but you will have created an invalid environment.\n"
"You would likely then see some of the other error messages described in this section.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Jika anda mendapat ralat ini, **jangan** cuba membina persekitaran dengan memanggil `pip install` beberapa kali.\n"
"Arahan-arahan tersebut mungkin tidak gagal, tetapi anda akan mencipta persekitaran yang tidak sah.\n"
"Anda kemudian mungkin akan melihat beberapa mesej ralat lain yang diterangkan dalam bahagian ini.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can also read [the documentation from the Python packaging authority "
"about conflict resolution](https://pip.pypa.io/en/latest/topics/dependency-"
"resolution/#dealing-with-dependency-conflicts).\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda juga boleh membaca [dokumentasi daripada Python packaging authority "
"tentang resolusi konflik](https://pip.pypa.io/en/latest/topics/dependency-"
"resolution/#dealing-with-dependency-conflicts).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`pip` succeeds but prints errors after running `pip install` commands {#pip-"
"succeeds-but-prints-errors-after-running-pip-install-commands}"
msgstr ""
"`pip` berjaya tetapi mencetak ralat selepas menjalankan arahan `pip install`"
" {#pip-succeeds-but-prints-errors-after-running-pip-install-commands}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You might see an error in the output of `pip`, such as the following:\n"
msgstr "Anda mungkin melihat ralat dalam output `pip`, seperti yang berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The top line usually appears verbatim (as of `pip` 23.3), but second line changes depending on the exact problem, and there may be several lines like it.\n"
"`pip` is likely to then indicate that it did whatever you wanted successfully, despite the error message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Baris pertama biasanya muncul secara verbatim (setakat `pip` 23.3), tetapi baris kedua berubah bergantung pada masalah yang tepat, dan mungkin terdapat beberapa baris seperti itu.\n"
"`pip` kemudian kemungkinan akan menunjukkan bahawa ia berjaya melakukan apa yang anda mahu, walaupun ada mesej ralat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This means that the environment is in conflict and you cannot be sure that it will work correctly.\n"
"To solve the problem, examine the list of messages from `pip` and determine if you need all of the packages that have conflicting requirements.\n"
"Sometimes there will be true conflicts between dependencies; you might need multiple virtual environments to separate out dependencies that have incompatible requirements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini bermakna persekitaran berada dalam konflik dan anda tidak boleh memastikan ia akan berfungsi dengan betul.\n"
"Untuk menyelesaikan masalah, periksa senarai mesej daripada `pip` dan tentukan sama ada anda memerlukan semua pakej yang mempunyai keperluan bercanggah.\n"
"Kadangkala akan ada konflik sebenar antara kebergantungan; anda mungkin memerlukan beberapa persekitaran maya untuk mengasingkan kebergantungan yang mempunyai keperluan tidak serasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The safest choice is to begin a new virtual environment (or more than one, "
"if there are true conflicts), then delete the one in conflict.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilihan paling selamat adalah memulakan persekitaran maya baharu (atau lebih"
" daripada satu, jika ada konflik sebenar), kemudian padam yang berada dalam "
"konflik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When setting up virtual environments, run only one `pip install` command that includes all the dependencies you need.\n"
"This is the most reliable way for `pip` to find a properly resolved environment with no conflicts.\n"
"If you keep having problems with conflicts after setting up environments, avoid running any further `pip install` or `pip uninstall` commands; `pip` does not guarantee to keep the environment coherent on subsequent commands.\n"
msgstr ""
"Semasa menyediakan persekitaran maya, jalankan hanya satu arahan `pip install` yang merangkumi semua kebergantungan yang anda perlukan.\n"
"Ini adalah cara paling boleh dipercayai untuk `pip` mencari persekitaran yang diselesaikan dengan betul tanpa konflik.\n"
"Jika anda terus menghadapi masalah dengan konflik selepas menyediakan persekitaran, elakkan menjalankan arahan `pip install` atau `pip uninstall` seterusnya; `pip` tidak menjamin untuk memastikan persekitaran kekal koheren pada arahan berikutnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"If you are concerned about working with multiple virtual environments, rest assured that Python development and use often involve several virtual environments. It's common and good practice to create new ones to work on separate projects.\n"
"When you're done with a virtual environment, you can simply delete its directory; there is no reason to keep multiple environments permanently.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Jika anda bimbang tentang bekerja dengan beberapa persekitaran maya, yakinlah bahawa pembangunan dan penggunaan Python sering melibatkan beberapa persekitaran maya. Adalah perkara biasa dan amalan baik untuk mencipta yang baharu bagi bekerja pada projek yang berasingan.\n"
"Apabila anda selesai dengan sesebuah persekitaran maya, anda boleh memadamnya sahaja; tiada sebab untuk menyimpan beberapa persekitaran secara kekal.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qiskit-1.0-import-error\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"qiskit-1.0-import-error\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`import qiskit` raises `ImportError` {#import-qiskit-raises-importerror}"
msgstr ""
"`import qiskit` menimbulkan `ImportError` {#import-qiskit-raises-"
"importerror}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "When running `import qiskit`, you might see an error such as:\n"
msgstr ""
"Semasa menjalankan `import qiskit`, anda mungkin melihat ralat seperti:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ImportError: Qiskit is installed in an invalid environment that has both Qiskit 1.0+ and an earlier version.\n"
" You should create a new virtual environment, and ensure that you do not mix dependencies between Qiskit pre-1.0 and post-1.0.\n"
" Any packages that depend on 'qiskit-terra' are not compatible with Qiskit 1.0 and will need to be updated.\n"
" Qiskit unfortunately cannot enforce this requirement during environment resolution.\n"
msgstr ""
" ImportError: Qiskit is installed in an invalid environment that has both Qiskit 1.0+ and an earlier version.\n"
" You should create a new virtual environment, and ensure that you do not mix dependencies between Qiskit pre-1.0 and post-1.0.\n"
" Any packages that depend on 'qiskit-terra' are not compatible with Qiskit 1.0 and will need to be updated.\n"
" Qiskit unfortunately cannot enforce this requirement during environment resolution.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"You might have run a completely valid `pip install` command, following all the recommendations in this guide, and still see this error message.\n"
"This is not your fault, but the error message is still correct, and Qiskit cannot safely load.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"Anda mungkin telah menjalankan arahan `pip install` yang sepenuhnya sah, mengikuti semua cadangan dalam panduan ini, dan masih melihat mesej ralat ini.\n"
"Ini bukan kesalahan anda, tetapi mesej ralat itu masih betul, dan Qiskit tidak dapat dimuatkan dengan selamat.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The error means that Qiskit is installed in an invalid environment that includes both Qiskit v1.0 and an earlier version.\n"
"This is characterized by the `qiskit-terra` distribution being installed alongside Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"You can check what distributions are installed by running `pip list`, but you cannot fix this by simply uninstalling `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ralat tersebut bermakna Qiskit dipasang dalam persekitaran yang tidak sah yang merangkumi kedua-dua Qiskit v1.0 dan versi sebelumnya.\n"
"Ini dicirikan oleh pengedaran `qiskit-terra` yang dipasang bersama Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Anda boleh menyemak pengedaran yang dipasang dengan menjalankan `pip list`, tetapi anda tidak boleh membetulkan ini dengan hanya menyahpasang `qiskit-terra`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, `qiskit>=1.0` and `qiskit-terra` are conflicting distributions, and cannot both be installed together.\n"
"Even more unfortunately, *we cannot communicate this conflict to `pip`* because of limitations in its metadata system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Malangnya, `qiskit>=1.0` dan `qiskit-terra` adalah pengedaran yang bercanggah, dan tidak boleh dipasang bersama-sama.\n"
"Lebih malang lagi, *kami tidak dapat menyampaikan konflik ini kepada `pip`* kerana had dalam sistem metadatanya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This error most frequently arises in one of two situations:\n"
msgstr "Ralat ini paling kerap timbul dalam salah satu daripada dua situasi:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '*  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You ran something like `pip install 'qiskit>=1' something-else`, and "
"`something-else` has a requirement on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda menjalankan sesuatu seperti `pip install 'qiskit>=1' something-else`, "
"dan `something-else` mempunyai keperluan pada `qiskit-terra`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '*  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You tried to run `pip install -U qiskit` in an existing environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda cuba menjalankan `pip install -U qiskit` dalam persekitaran sedia "
"ada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In both of these cases, there is no guarantee that `pip` will return a "
"helpful message to you.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kedua-dua kes ini, tiada jaminan bahawa `pip` akan mengembalikan mesej"
" yang berguna kepada anda.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"tip\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"tip\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to require `pip` to forbid `qiskit-terra` from individual `install` commands is to use [a constraints file](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/user_guide/#constraints-files) that requires that `qiskit-terra` is set to an impossible version.\n"
"For example, a constraints file that includes the line `qiskit-terra>=1.0` will mean that if a dependency attempts to install `qiskit-terra`, no published versions will match the requirements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Salah satu cara untuk meminta `pip` melarang `qiskit-terra` daripada arahan `install` individu adalah dengan menggunakan [fail kekangan](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/user_guide/#constraints-files) yang menetapkan `qiskit-terra` pada versi yang mustahil.\n"
"Contohnya, fail kekangan yang mengandungi baris `qiskit-terra>=1.0` bermakna jika kebergantungan cuba memasang `qiskit-terra`, tiada versi yang diterbitkan akan memenuhi keperluan tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We have provided such a file in a GitHub Gist at "
"[https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints](https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints), which "
"you can use like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kami telah menyediakan fail sedemikian dalam GitHub Gist di "
"[https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints](https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints), yang "
"boleh anda gunakan seperti berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If a package requires `qiskit-terra`, you will see [a resolution "
"failure](#pip-resolution-impossible).\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika sesebuah pakej memerlukan `qiskit-terra`, anda akan melihat [kegagalan "
"resolusi](#pip-resolution-impossible).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr "</DoqAdmonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"debug-venv-for-1.0\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"debug-venv-for-1.0\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create a working environment for Qiskit v1.0 {#create-a-working-environment-"
"for-qiskit-v10}"
msgstr ""
"Cipta persekitaran yang berfungsi untuk Qiskit v1.0 {#create-a-working-"
"environment-for-qiskit-v10}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"No matter how this happened, it is much easier to make a new virtual "
"environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tidak kira bagaimana ini berlaku, adalah lebih mudah untuk membuat "
"persekitaran maya baharu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we need to find out which packages are introducing a dependency on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
"Using the broken environment, install `pipdeptree` from PyPI. This is a tool for generating dependency graphs:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, kita perlu mengetahui pakej mana yang memperkenalkan kebergantungan pada `qiskit-terra`.\n"
"Menggunakan persekitaran yang rosak, pasang `pipdeptree` daripada PyPI. Ini adalah alat untuk menjana graf kebergantungan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Ask it which packages are introducing dependencies on `qiskit-terra` and "
"`qiskit` (these are two separate commands):\n"
msgstr ""
"Tanya ia pakej mana yang memperkenalkan kebergantungan pada `qiskit-terra` "
"dan `qiskit` (ini adalah dua arahan berasingan):\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The outputs might look something like:\n"
msgstr "Outputnya mungkin kelihatan seperti:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the above example, we have two distributions that have declared "
"themselves compatible with Qiskit v1.0 (`qiskit-aer` and `qiskit-ibm-"
"provider`), and one that still has a dependency on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam contoh di atas, kita mempunyai dua pengedaran yang telah "
"mengisytiharkan diri serasi dengan Qiskit v1.0 (`qiskit-aer` dan `qiskit-"
"ibm-provider`), dan satu yang masih mempunyai kebergantungan pada `qiskit-"
"terra`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"This example is a flat dependency structure.\n"
"You might see a much deeper tree than this.\n"
"The packages that are directly dependent on `qiskit-terra` (lowest indentation) are most likely to be the problematic ones, but one farther down the tree could be problematic if it depends on a specific old version of some other package that has already been updated.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"Contoh ini adalah struktur kebergantungan rata.\n"
"Anda mungkin melihat pokok yang jauh lebih dalam daripada ini.\n"
"Pakej yang bergantung secara langsung pada `qiskit-terra` (indentasi paling rendah) kemungkinan besar adalah yang bermasalah, tetapi satu yang lebih jauh ke bawah pokok boleh menjadi bermasalah jika ia bergantung pada versi lama tertentu bagi pakej lain yang telah pun dikemaskini.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Seeing a dependency on `qiskit-terra` can mean one of a few things:\n"
msgstr ""
"Melihat kebergantungan pada `qiskit-terra` boleh bermakna salah satu "
"daripada beberapa perkara:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The dependent is an old package, and will not be updated to support Qiskit "
"v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pakej yang bergantung adalah pakej lama, dan tidak akan dikemaskini untuk "
"menyokong Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  In this case, there is no chance of using the package with Qiskit v1.0, and you will need to continue using a previous version of Qiskit.\n"
"  Typically this is characterized by the dependent being at its latest version (assuming the environment is new, and you didn't pin it lower) and having a direct requirement on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Dalam kes ini, tiada kemungkinan untuk menggunakan pakej tersebut dengan Qiskit v1.0, dan anda perlu terus menggunakan versi Qiskit yang sebelumnya.\n"
"  Biasanya ini dicirikan oleh pakej yang bergantung berada pada versi terbarunya (dengan mengandaikan persekitaran adalah baharu, dan anda tidak meletakkan pin pada versi yang lebih rendah) dan mempunyai keperluan langsung pada `qiskit-terra`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The dependent is a package that is actively maintained, but does not yet "
"support Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pakej yang bergantung adalah pakej yang diselenggara secara aktif, tetapi "
"belum menyokong Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  In this case, you will need to wait for the developers to release a compatible version - please be patient!\n"
"  Typically this is characterized by the installed distribution *not* being at its latest version, even though your installation command did not specify a version.\n"
"  You can check the latest release version of the distribution by finding its page on https://pypi.org/.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Dalam kes ini, anda perlu menunggu pembangun mengeluarkan versi yang serasi — sila bersabar!\n"
"  Biasanya ini dicirikan oleh pengedaran yang dipasang *bukan* berada pada versi terbarunya, walaupun arahan pemasangan anda tidak menentukan versi.\n"
"  Anda boleh menyemak versi pelepasan terkini pengedaran dengan mencari halamannya di https://pypi.org/.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  `pip` likely searched old versions of the package until it found one "
"(possibly from months or years ago) that depended only on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"  `pip` kemungkinan mencari versi lama pakej sehingga ia menemukan satu "
"(mungkin dari bulan atau tahun lalu) yang hanya bergantung pada `qiskit-"
"terra`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  This is what has happened in the example above.  At the time this document"
" was created, `qiskit-dynamics==0.4.4` was the latest release version.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Inilah yang berlaku dalam contoh di atas. Pada masa dokumen ini dibuat, "
"`qiskit-dynamics==0.4.4` adalah versi pelepasan terkini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you constructed this environment out of several `pip install` commands (such as if the environment is old and has been updated), first try to install all of your packages by using a single `pip install` command when you build a new environment.\n"
"If the problem persists, at least one of the packages you want likely does not support Qiskit v1.0 yet, and `pip` is finding an old version that it believes will work because it doesn't know about the `qiskit>=1`/`qiskit-terra` conflict.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika anda membina persekitaran ini daripada beberapa arahan `pip install` (seperti jika persekitaran itu lama dan telah dikemaskini), cuba dahulu memasang semua pakej anda menggunakan satu arahan `pip install` semasa anda membina persekitaran baharu.\n"
"Jika masalah berterusan, sekurang-kurangnya satu daripada pakej yang anda mahu mungkin belum menyokong Qiskit v1.0 lagi, dan `pip` sedang mencari versi lama yang ia percaya akan berfungsi kerana ia tidak tahu tentang konflik `qiskit>=1`/`qiskit-terra`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Instead, use the `pipdeptree` commands to identify which dependencies do not yet support Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Exclude any packages that do not yet support Qiskit v1.0 when constructing a Qiskit v1.0 environment, or continue to use a prior version of Qiskit.\n"
"See [Create the new environment](#creating-a-venv) for instructions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebaliknya, gunakan arahan `pipdeptree` untuk mengenal pasti kebergantungan yang belum menyokong Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Kecualikan sebarang pakej yang belum menyokong Qiskit v1.0 semasa membina persekitaran Qiskit v1.0, atau terus gunakan versi Qiskit yang sebelumnya.\n"
"Lihat [Cipta persekitaran baharu](#creating-a-venv) untuk arahan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The example in this section was generated before Qiskit v1.0 was released.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Contoh dalam bahagian ini dijana sebelum Qiskit v1.0 dikeluarkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The \"old\" distribution in question (`qiskit-dynamics`) was behaving correctly; it was not known to support Qiskit v1.0 yet, so it marked that in its requirements.\n"
"It's not possible to backdate requirements changes to previously released versions, and `pip` will search arbitrarily far back to locate something that works when building an environment.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengedaran \"lama\" yang dimaksudkan (`qiskit-dynamics`) berkelakuan dengan betul; ia belum diketahui menyokong Qiskit v1.0 lagi, jadi ia menandakan perkara itu dalam keperluannya.\n"
"Tidak mungkin untuk mengubah keperluan dengan tarikh ke versi yang telah dikeluarkan sebelumnya, dan `pip` akan mencari sejauh mungkin ke belakang untuk menemukan sesuatu yang berfungsi semasa membina persekitaran.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"debug-venv-for-0.45\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"debug-venv-for-0.45\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create a working environment for Qiskit 0.45 or 0.46 {#create-a-working-"
"environment-for-qiskit-045-or-046}"
msgstr ""
"Cipta persekitaran yang berfungsi untuk Qiskit 0.45 atau 0.46 {#create-a-"
"working-environment-for-qiskit-045-or-046}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you have a broken environment after trying to install Qiskit 0.45 or 0.46, the most likely situation is that `pip` installed Qiskit v1.0 because it tried to pick the latest versions of packages, even though it was not required.\n"
"The easiest way to fix this is to create a new virtual environment, then run a single `pip install` command that has all the packages you need, plus an explicit `'qiskit<1'` entry.\n"
"If `pip` successfully resolves this dependency graph, you should have a working virtual environment.\n"
"If at least one distribution requires Qiskit v1.0 or greater, `pip` should give you an error message explaining this, which looks like the one in [the section on failed resolutions](#pip-resolution-impossible).\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika anda mempunyai persekitaran yang rosak selepas cuba memasang Qiskit 0.45 atau 0.46, situasi yang paling berkemungkinan adalah bahawa `pip` memasang Qiskit v1.0 kerana ia cuba memilih versi terkini pakej, walaupun ia tidak diperlukan.\n"
"Cara termudah untuk membetulkannya adalah dengan mencipta persekitaran maya baharu, kemudian menjalankan satu arahan `pip install` yang merangkumi semua pakej yang anda perlukan, ditambah entri eksplisit `'qiskit<1'`.\n"
"Jika `pip` berjaya menyelesaikan graf kebergantungan ini, anda sepatutnya mempunyai persekitaran maya yang berfungsi.\n"
"Jika sekurang-kurangnya satu pengedaran memerlukan Qiskit v1.0 atau lebih tinggi, `pip` sepatutnya memberikan anda mesej ralat yang menjelaskan ini, yang kelihatan seperti yang ada dalam [bahagian tentang resolusi yang gagal](#pip-resolution-impossible).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can also use the `pipdeptree` commands listed in [Create a working "
"environment for Qiskit 1.0](#debug-venv-for-1.0) from within the broken "
"environment to determine which distributions have an explicit requirement on"
" `qiskit>=1`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda juga boleh menggunakan arahan `pipdeptree` yang disenaraikan dalam "
"[Cipta persekitaran yang berfungsi untuk Qiskit 1.0](#debug-venv-for-1.0) "
"dari dalam persekitaran yang rosak untuk menentukan pengedaran yang "
"mempunyai keperluan eksplisit pada `qiskit>=1`.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"I'm a developer, my environments are definitely right, and I'm still getting"
" the error {#im-a-developer-my-environments-are-definitely-right-and-im-"
"still-getting-the-error}"
msgstr ""
"Saya seorang pembangun, persekitaran saya pasti betul, dan saya masih "
"mendapat ralat {#im-a-developer-my-environments-are-definitely-right-and-im-"
"still-getting-the-error}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First: you must be *absolutely* certain that your environments are correct.\n"
"The test that Qiskit uses to determine a broken environment is quite robust; specifically, it queries `importlib.metadata` for distribution information on installed packages and checks the version numbers returned.\n"
"The Qiskit v1.0 side of the test also checks for sentinel files that were present in old Qiskit versions and not Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama: anda mesti *benar-benar* pasti bahawa persekitaran anda betul.\n"
"Ujian yang digunakan Qiskit untuk menentukan persekitaran yang rosak adalah cukup teguh; khususnya, ia membuat pertanyaan kepada `importlib.metadata` untuk maklumat pengedaran tentang pakej yang dipasang dan menyemak nombor versi yang dikembalikan.\n"
"Bahagian Qiskit v1.0 dalam ujian juga menyemak fail sentinel yang ada dalam versi Qiskit lama dan bukan Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are a Qiskit developer, it's possible that you have old `qiskit.egg-info` or `qiskit-terra.egg-info` (or `*.dist-info`) directories present on your meta path (see `sys.meta_path`), left over from old editable installations.\n"
"In particular, check your working directory for any `*.egg-info` and `*.dist-info` directories.\n"
"If they're in the root of one of your checked out repositories, you can delete them. The worst that can happen is you might need to `pip install -e .` again, and even that is unlikely, because these are typically just part of the `setuptools` build process that doesn't get cleaned up.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika anda adalah pembangun Qiskit, ada kemungkinan anda mempunyai direktori `qiskit.egg-info` atau `qiskit-terra.egg-info` lama (atau `*.dist-info`) yang terdapat pada laluan meta anda (lihat `sys.meta_path`), tinggalan daripada pemasangan boleh edit lama.\n"
"Khususnya, semak direktori kerja anda untuk sebarang direktori `*.egg-info` dan `*.dist-info`.\n"
"Jika ia berada di akar salah satu repositori yang anda daftar keluar, anda boleh memadamnya. Perkara terburuk yang boleh berlaku adalah anda mungkin perlu menjalankan `pip install -e .` semula, dan walaupun itu tidak mungkin, kerana ini biasanya hanya merupakan sebahagian daripada proses binaan `setuptools` yang tidak dibersihkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the above information does not help you and you are 100% sure that your "
"environment is sound (or you are deliberately trying to test a broken "
"environment):\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika maklumat di atas tidak membantu anda dan anda 100% pasti persekitaran "
"anda baik (atau anda sengaja cuba menguji persekitaran yang rosak):\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Create an issue in "
"Qiskit](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/issues/new/choose) explaining how "
"this happened and why you are sure the environment is correct so we can fix "
"it.\n"
msgstr ""
"[Cipta isu dalam Qiskit](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/issues/new/choose)"
" menerangkan bagaimana ini berlaku dan mengapa anda pasti persekitaran itu "
"betul supaya kami dapat membetulkannya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can suppress the exception by setting the environment variable "
"`QISKIT_SUPPRESS_1_0_IMPORT_ERROR=1`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda boleh menekan pengecualian dengan menetapkan pemboleh ubah persekitaran"
" `QISKIT_SUPPRESS_1_0_IMPORT_ERROR=1`.\n"
